WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.509
Long before he started collecting Infinity
Stones in the MCU and laid waste to the Avengers

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:09.240
in Infinity War, comics readers were well
aware that Thanos is undoubtedly one of the

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.600
strongest beings in the Marvel Universe.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.040
But you know what they say: the bigger they
are, the harder they fall, and nobody has

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.800
fallen harder than The Mad Titan.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:17.980
"Who dead?

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.480
You dead!"

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.060
"you dead, yes!"

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.140
How?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.420
Here's a look at seven Marvel characters who
have single-handedly destroyed Thanos.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.100
Drax the Destroyer

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.140
"of course Ronan was only a puppet."

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.260
Considering he was literally created to destroy
Thanos, Drax the Destroyer has a pretty poor

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.300
track record, getting defeated time and time
again.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.700
"You had one job."

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.740
But in Annihilation #4, Drax finally managed
to take Thanos out, punching him right through

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.840
the chest and literally ripping his heart
out.

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:52.879
Of course, he did it at exactly the wrong
time, as Thanos had just teamed up with the

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.940
good guys to save the universe from the villainous
Annihilus.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.600
That's just soooo Drax.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.180
Adam Warlock

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.980
The full power of the Infinity Gems was on
display in 1977's Marvel Two-in-One Annual

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.730
#2, where Thanos attempted use their might
to destroy the sun.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.940
The combined power of the Avengers and their
allies wasn't enough to stop him, but luckily

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.840
they had an inside man - literally.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.280
Contained inside the Soul Gem was the spirit
of Thanos's arch-enemy, Adam Warlock.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.020
Once freed, he made short work of Thanos by
turning him into solid rock.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.860
Hey, he said he wanted stones, right?!

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:26.680
Thane

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:32.610
Early in Thanos' life, the Mad Titan killed
his mother, his wife, his children, and countless

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.980
millions more in the hopes of persuading Mistress
Death to love him and become his wife.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.700
Years later, though, during the Infinity crossover
event, readers discovered that during his

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.440
travels, Thanos fathered an Inhuman/Eternal
hybrid son named Thane.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.680
In Infinity #6, Thanos finds his son, intent
on killing him too.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.480
However, Thanos is betrayed by his minion
Ebony Maw, who harnesses Thane's innate power

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.820
over death itself to freeze Thanos in a amber-like
prison known as "Living Death."

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:00.700
Zombie Hulk

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.720
Who doesn't like zombies, right?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.290
Marvel certainly does, because starting in
2005, they began a series of Marvel Zombies

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.880
storylines featuring the Marvel heroes and
villains all turned into brain-eating zombies.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.760
Written by Walking Dead creator Robert Kirkman
himself, Marvel Zombies 2 took place 40 years

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.920
in the future, after super zombies have eaten
their way across the entire universe.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.420
Among those left: Zombie Thanos and Zombie
Hulk.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.840
And if you think Hulk Smashes, imagine how
much smashing Zombie Hulk does - something

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.220
that Thanos learned the hard way when he made
the mistake of getting Hulk angry.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.640
Hey, he did warn us!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.140
"That's my secret, Captain.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.040
I'm always angry."

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:40.980
Death

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.280
The first issue of Thanos' 2016 ongoing solo
series ended with the revelation that Thanos,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.170
though at the height of his power to all outward
appearance, was dying from a debilitating

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.720
illness that left him weak and eventually
powerless.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.580
So where did this mystery malady come from?

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.200
In Thanos #6, fans learned that it was inflicted
by none other than Death herself.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.500
And who can blame her after having to endure
decades of clearly unwanted advances from

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.720
a petulant, entitled jerk like Thanos?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.000
She's not into you, bro!

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.640
With his powers gone, Thanos was left vulnerable
for a series of vicious beatdowns, each and

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.540
every one of which he totally had coming.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.380
"My lady!

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.860
Protect me!"

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:22.700
Himself

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.160
In the classic series Infinity Gauntlet, which
inspired the hit film Avengers: Infinity War,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.580
Thanos outdid himself, killing half the universe
in another failed attempt to impress Death.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:36.900
And with the power to control all reality
with the Infinity Gauntlet, it seemed as though

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.620
nothing could stop his childish anger.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.580
But it turned out there was someone who could
defeat Thanos: himself.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.420
Yes, old pal Adam Warlock revealed to Thanos
that through a psychic bond, he learned that

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.420
Thanos secretly knows he's not worthy of the
power he seeks, and thus always unconsciously

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.980
makes mistakes allowing himself to be defeated.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.340
Realizing the truth in Warlock's words, Thanos
helped Warlock regain the Infinity Gauntlet

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.560
and restore the universe.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.560
Squirrel Girl

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.880
Finally, no list of the Marvel Universe's
most powerful characters would be complete

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.880
with Squirrel Girl.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.340
She has the powers of both a squirrel and
a girl, making her unbeatable.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.180
Don't believe us?

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:16.680
Just ask Dr. Doom, or Galactus, both of whom
she has defeated using pluck, self confidence,

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.260
friendship, and - of course - the help of
her squirrel friends.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.080
Just how awesome is Squirrel Girl?

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.280
In the GLX-Mas Special one-shot, Squirrel
Girl defeated Thanos with the help of her

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.080
trusted squirrel, Tippy-Toe, thereby saving
the entire Multiverse.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.340
And in total badass style, she did it off
panel, because it's such a given she would

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.520
win that it's not even worth the time to show
it.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:39.900
Maybe if he had used the Thanos-copter instead
of the Infinity Gauntlet he would have won.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.420
Thanks for watching!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.340
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.660
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

